{"id":"mahabharata-3-157","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":157,"title":"सप्तपञ्चाशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 157 · Bhima kills Maniman","summary":{"en":"The Pandavas live at Arshtishena's hermitage. Urged by Draupadi, who longs to see the peak cleared of demons, Bhima climbs to Kubera's city and slaughters the Yakshas and Rakshasas, killing their leader Maniman.","kn":"ಪಾಂಡವರು ಆರ್ಷ್ಟಿಷೇಣನ ಆಶ್ರಮದಲ್ಲಿ ವಾಸಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಶಿಖರವನ್ನು ರಾಕ್ಷಸರಿಂದ ಮುಕ್ತವಾಗಿ ಕಾಣಲು ಬಯಸಿದ ದ್ರೌಪದಿಯ ಪ್ರೇರಣೆಯಿಂದ ಭೀಮನು ಕುಬೇರನ ನಗರಕ್ಕೇರಿ ಯಕ್ಷ ರಾಕ್ಷಸರನ್ನು ಸಂಹರಿಸಿ ಅವರ ನಾಯಕ ಮಣಿಮಂತನನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"पाण्डव आर्ष्टिषेण के आश्रम में रहते हैं। शिखर को राक्षसों से मुक्त देखने की इच्छुक द्रौपदी के उकसाने पर भीम कुबेर की नगरी तक चढ़कर यक्षों और राक्षसों का संहार करते हैं और उनके नायक मणिमान को मार डालते हैं।","te":"పాండవులు ఆర్ష్టిషేణుని ఆశ్రమంలో నివసిస్తారు. శిఖరాన్ని రాక్షసరహితంగా చూడాలనుకున్న ద్రౌపది ప్రేరణతో భీముడు కుబేరుని నగరానికి ఎక్కి యక్షులను, రాక్షసులను సంహరించి వారి నాయకుడు మణిమంతుని చంపుతాడు.","ta":"பாண்டவர்கள் ஆர்ஷ்டிஷேணரின் ஆசிரமத்தில் வாழ்கிறார்கள். சிகரத்தை அரக்கர்கள் இல்லாமல் காண விரும்பிய திரௌபதியின் தூண்டுதலால் பீமன் குபேரனின் நகருக்கு ஏறி யக்ஷர்களையும் அரக்கர்களையும் கொன்று அவர்கள் தலைவன் மணிமானைக் கொல்கிறான்.","ml":"പാണ്ഡവർ അർഷ്ടിഷേണന്റെ ആശ്രമത്തിൽ വസിക്കുന്നു. കൊടുമുടി രാക്ഷസരിൽനിന്ന് മുക്തമാകാൻ ആഗ്രഹിക്കുന്ന ദ്രൗപദിയുടെ പ്രേരണയാൽ ഭീമൻ കുബേരന്റെ നഗരത്തിലേക്ക് കയറി യക്ഷന്മാരെയും രാക്ഷസന്മാരെയും വധിക്കുന്നു; അവരുടെ നേതാവ് മണിമാനെയും അദ്ദേഹം കൊല്ലുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.157; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"यक्षयुद्धपर्व","titleEn":"Yakshayuddha Parva (Battle with the Yakshas)","verses":[{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"पाण्डोः पुत्रा महात्मानः सर्वे दिव्यपराक्रमाः ।\nकियन्तं कालमवसन्पर्वते गन्धमादने ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the great-souled sons of Pandu had divine valour. How long did they live on Mount Gandhamadana?"}},{"n":2,"text":"कानि चाभ्यवहार्याणि तत्र तेषां महात्मनाम् ।\nवसतां लोकवीराणामासंस्तद्ब्रूहि सत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell me, best of men, what food those great-souled heroes of the world had while they lived there."}},{"n":3,"text":"विस्तरेण च मे शंस भीमसेनपराक्रमम् ।\nयद्यच्चक्रे महाबाहुस्तस्मिन्हैमवते गिरौ ।\nन खल्वासीत्पुनर्युद्धं तस्य यक्षैर्द्विजोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell me in detail of the prowess of Bhimasena, and of whatever the mighty-armed one did on that Himalayan mountain. Was there no fighting again with the Yakshas, best of brahmins?"}},{"n":4,"text":"कच्चित्समागमस्तेषामासीद्वैश्रवणेन च ।\nतत्र ह्यायाति धनद आर्ष्टिषेणो यथाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Did they meet Vaishravana? For the giver of wealth comes there, as Arshtishena said."}},{"n":5,"text":"एतदिच्छाम्यहं श्रोतुं विस्तरेण तपोधन ।\nन हि मे शृण्वतस्तृप्तिरस्ति तेषां विचेष्टितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I want to hear this in detail, rich in austerity. I am never satisfied hearing their deeds."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"एतदात्महितं श्रुत्वा तस्याप्रतिमतेजसः ।\nशासनं सततं चक्रुस्तथैव भरतर्षभाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard this beneficial counsel of that sage of matchless radiance, the bulls of the Bharatas always followed his instruction."}},{"n":7,"text":"भुञ्जाना मुनिभोज्यानि रसवन्ति फलानि च ।\nशुद्धबाणहतानां च मृगाणां पिशितान्यपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"They ate the food of sages, juicy fruits, and the flesh of deer killed by clean arrows."}},{"n":8,"text":"मेध्यानि हिमवत्पृष्ठे मधूनि विविधानि च ।\nएवं ते न्यवसंस्तत्र पाण्डवा भरतर्षभाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They ate pure honeys of many kinds on the back of the Himalaya. So those bulls of the Bharatas lived there."}},{"n":9,"text":"तथा निवसतां तेषां पञ्चमं वर्षमभ्यगात् ।\nशृण्वतां लोमशोक्तानि वाक्यानि विविधानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"While they lived thus, listening to Lomasha's many accounts, the fifth year came."}},{"n":10,"text":"कृत्यकाल उपस्थास्य इति चोक्त्वा घटोत्कचः ।\nराक्षसैः सहितः सर्वैः पूर्वमेव गतः प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ghatotkacha, saying, \"I shall appear when it is time to act,\" had gone off earlier with all the rakshasas, lord."}},{"n":11,"text":"आर्ष्टिषेणाश्रमे तेषां वसतां वै महात्मनाम् ।\nअगच्छन्बहवो मासाः पश्यतां महदद्भुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many months passed for those great-souled ones living in Arshtishena's hermitage, watching a great marvel."}},{"n":12,"text":"तैस्तत्र रममाणैश्च विहरद्भिश्च पाण्डवैः ।\nप्रीतिमन्तो महाभागा मुनयश्चारणास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"While the Pandavas lived and played there, sages and Charanas, greatly fortunate and pleased, came,"}},{"n":13,"text":"आजग्मुः पाण्डवान्द्रष्टुं सिद्धात्मानो यतव्रताः ।\nतैस्तैः सह कथाश्चक्रुर्दिव्या भरतसत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Siddhas of self-control and firm vows, to see the Pandavas, and the best of the Bharatas held divine talk with them."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततः कतिपयाहस्य महाह्रदनिवासिनम् ।\nऋद्धिमन्तं महानागं सुपर्णः सहसाहरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some days later Garuda suddenly carried off a prosperous great serpent that dwelt in a great lake."}},{"n":15,"text":"प्राकम्पत महाशैलः प्रामृद्यन्त महाद्रुमाः ।\nददृशुः सर्वभूतानि पाण्डवाश्च तदद्भुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great mountain shook and great trees were crushed. All creatures and the Pandavas saw that marvel."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततः शैलोत्तमस्याग्रात्पाण्डवान्प्रति मारुतः ।\nअवहत्सर्वमाल्यानि गन्धवन्ति शुभानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then from the top of the best of mountains the wind carried toward the Pandavas fragrant, lovely garlands of every kind."}},{"n":17,"text":"तत्र पुष्पाणि दिव्यानि सुहृद्भिः सह पाण्डवाः ।\nददृशुः पञ्च वर्णानि द्रौपदी च यशस्विनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the Pandavas, with their friends, and renowned Draupadi, saw divine flowers of five colours."}},{"n":18,"text":"भीमसेनं ततः कृष्णा काले वचनमब्रवीत् ।\nविविक्ते पर्वतोद्देशे सुखासीनं महाभुजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then at the proper time Krishna Draupadi spoke to Bhimasena, as he sat at ease, mighty-armed, in a secluded part of the mountain."}},{"n":19,"text":"सुपर्णानिलवेगेन श्वसनेन महाबलात् ।\nपञ्चवर्णानि पात्यन्ते पुष्पाणि भरतर्षभ ।\nप्रत्यक्षं सर्वभूतानां नदीमश्वरथां प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Bull of the Bharatas, by the force of the wind from Suparna, flowers of five colours are being dropped, before the eyes of all creatures, toward the river Ashvaratha.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"खाण्डवे सत्यसंधेन भ्रात्रा तव नरेश्वर ।\nगन्धर्वोरगरक्षांसि वासवश्च निवारितः ।\nहता मायाविनश्चोग्रा धनुः प्राप्तं च गाण्डिवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"At Khandava, your brother, true to his word, king, held off the Gandharvas, serpents, rakshasas and Vasava himself; he killed the fierce illusionists and won Gandiva.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"तवापि सुमहत्तेजो महद्बाहुबलं च ते ।\nअविषह्यमनाधृष्यं शतक्रतुबलोपमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You too have very great energy and great strength of arm, unbearable and unassailable, like the might of Indra.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"त्वद्बाहुबलवेगेन त्रासिताः सर्वराक्षसाः ।\nहित्वा शैलं प्रपद्यन्तां भीमसेन दिशो दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let all the rakshasas, terrified by the speed of your arms' strength, leave this mountain and flee to the ten directions, Bhimasena.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"ततः शैलोत्तमस्याग्रं चित्रमाल्यधरं शिवम् ।\nव्यपेतभयसंमोहाः पश्यन्तु सुहृदस्तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Then let your friends, free of fear and confusion, see the summit of the best of mountains, with its wonderful garlands and its beauty.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"एवं प्रणिहितं भीम चिरात्प्रभृति मे मनः ।\nद्रष्टुमिच्छामि शैलाग्रं त्वद्बाहुबलमाश्रिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Bhima, my mind has long been set on this: I wish to see the mountain's summit, relying on the strength of your arms.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"ततः क्षिप्तमिवात्मानं द्रौपद्या स परंतपः ।\nनामृष्यत महाबाहुः प्रहारमिव सद्गवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi's words stung that tamer of foes, and the mighty-armed one could not bear it, like a fine bull a blow."}},{"n":26,"text":"सिंहर्षभगतिः श्रीमानुदारः कनकप्रभः ।\nमनस्वी बलवान्दृप्तो मानी शूरश्च पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Glorious, noble, golden in splendour, with the gait of a lion or bull, the Pandava was spirited, strong, proud, honourable and brave."}},{"n":27,"text":"लोहिताक्षः पृथुव्यंसो मत्तवारणविक्रमः ।\nसिंहदंष्ट्रो बृहत्स्कन्धः शालपोत इवोद्गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Red-eyed, broad-shouldered, with the stride of a rutting elephant, lion-fanged, thick-necked, tall as a young sala tree,"}},{"n":28,"text":"महात्मा चारुसर्वाङ्गः कम्बुग्रीवो महाभुजः ।\nरुक्मपृष्ठं धनुः खड्गं तूणांश्चापि परामृशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the great one, fair in every limb, conch-necked, long-armed, took up his gold-backed bow, sword and quivers."}},{"n":29,"text":"केसरीव यथोत्सिक्तः प्रभिन्न इव वारणः ।\nव्यपेतभयसंमोहः शैलमभ्यपतद्बली ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like a lion in heat or a rutting elephant, free from fear and confusion, the strong one rushed at the mountain."}},{"n":30,"text":"तं मृगेन्द्रमिवायान्तं प्रभिन्नमिव वारणम् ।\nददृशुः सर्वभूतानि बाणखड्गधनुर्धरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All creatures saw him coming, like a king of beasts or a rutting elephant, bearing arrows, sword and bow."}},{"n":31,"text":"द्रौपद्या वर्धयन्हर्षं गदामादाय पाण्डवः ।\nव्यपेतभयसंमोहः शैलराजं समाविशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Increasing Draupadi's delight, the Pandava took his mace and, free from fear and confusion, entered the king of mountains."}},{"n":32,"text":"न ग्लानिर्न च कातर्यं न वैक्लव्यं न मत्सरः ।\nकदाचिज्जुषते पार्थमात्मजं मातरिश्वनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither exhaustion, nor faintheartedness, nor distress, nor envy ever touches Partha, son of the Wind."}},{"n":33,"text":"तदेकायनमासाद्य विषमं भीमदर्शनम् ।\nबहुतालोच्छ्रयं शृङ्गमारुरोह महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He took the single path, uneven and fearful to see, and the mighty one climbed to a peak as high as many palm trees."}},{"n":34,"text":"स किंनरमहानागमुनिगन्धर्वराक्षसान् ।\nहर्षयन्पर्वतस्याग्रमाससाद महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gladdening Kinnaras, great serpents, sages, Gandharvas and rakshasas, the mighty one reached the top of the mountain."}},{"n":35,"text":"तत्र वैश्रवणावासं ददर्श भरतर्षभः ।\nकाञ्चनैः स्फाटिकाकारैर्वेश्मभिः समलंकृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the bull of the Bharatas saw Vaishravana's abode, adorned with golden houses shaped like crystal."}},{"n":36,"text":"मोदयन्सर्वभूतानि गन्धमादनसंभवः ।\nसर्वगन्धवहस्तत्र मारुतः सुसुखो ववौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Born of Gandhamadana, a most pleasant wind, bearing every fragrance, blew there, delighting all beings."}},{"n":37,"text":"चित्रा विविधवर्णाभाश्चित्रमञ्जरिधारिणः ।\nअचिन्त्या विविधास्तत्र द्रुमाः परमशोभनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were wondrous trees of many colours, wearing marvellous clusters of blossom, inconceivable and of the greatest beauty."}},{"n":38,"text":"रत्नजालपरिक्षिप्तं चित्रमाल्यधरं शिवम् ।\nराक्षसाधिपतेः स्थानं ददर्श भरतर्षभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The bull of the Bharatas saw the place of the lord of rakshasas, hung with nets of jewels and wearing marvellous garlands, auspicious."}},{"n":39,"text":"गदाखड्गधनुष्पाणिः समभित्यक्तजीवितः ।\nभीमसेनो महाबाहुस्तस्थौ गिरिरिवाचलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With mace, sword and bow in hand, having given up all regard for life, mighty-armed Bhimasena stood like an unmoving mountain."}},{"n":40,"text":"ततः शङ्खमुपाध्मासीद्द्विषतां लोमहर्षणम् ।\nज्याघोषतलघोषं च कृत्वा भूतान्यमोहयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he blew his conch, which makes the hair of enemies stand on end, and with the twang of his bowstring and the slap of his palms bewildered the creatures."}},{"n":41,"text":"ततः संहृष्टरोमाणः शब्दं तमभिदुद्रुवुः ।\nयक्षराक्षसगन्धर्वाः पाण्डवस्य समीपतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yakshas, rakshasas and Gandharvas, their hair bristling, rushed toward the Pandava, to that sound."}},{"n":42,"text":"गदापरिघनिस्त्रिंशशक्तिशूलपरश्वधाः ।\nप्रगृहीता व्यरोचन्त यक्षराक्षसबाहुभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Maces, iron clubs, swords, spears, tridents and axes, taken in the arms of Yakshas and rakshasas, shone."}},{"n":43,"text":"ततः प्रववृते युद्धं तेषां तस्य च भारत ।\nतैः प्रयुक्तान्महाकायैः शक्तिशूलपरश्वधान् ।\nभल्लैर्भीमः प्रचिच्छेद भीमवेगतरैस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then fighting broke out between them and him, Bharata. Bhima cut the spears, tridents and axes hurled by those huge-bodied ones with broad arrows of still more terrible speed."}},{"n":44,"text":"अन्तरिक्षचराणां च भूमिष्ठानां च गर्जताम् ।\nशरैर्विव्याध गात्राणि राक्षसानां महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty one pierced with arrows the bodies of the roaring rakshasas, both those flying in the air and those on the ground."}},{"n":45,"text":"सा लोहितमहावृष्टिरभ्यवर्षन्महाबलम् ।\nकायेभ्यः प्रच्युता धारा राक्षसानां समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A great rain of blood fell on the mighty one, streams pouring from the bodies of the rakshasas on every side."}},{"n":46,"text":"भीमबाहुबलोत्सृष्टैर्बहुधा यक्षरक्षसाम् ।\nविनिकृत्तान्यदृश्यन्त शरीराणि शिरांसि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bodies and heads of Yakshas and rakshasas, cut off in many ways by the strength of Bhima's arms, were seen."}},{"n":47,"text":"प्रच्छाद्यमानं रक्षोभिः पाण्डवं प्रियदर्शनम् ।\nददृशुः सर्वभूतानि सूर्यमभ्रगणैरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"All creatures saw the lovely Pandava being covered by the rakshasas, like the sun by masses of cloud."}},{"n":48,"text":"स रश्मिभिरिवादित्यः शरैररिनिघातिभिः ।\nसर्वानार्छन्महाबाहुर्बलवान्सत्यविक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like the sun with its rays, the mighty-armed, strong, truly valiant one cut down all of them with arrows that smote his foes."}},{"n":49,"text":"अभितर्जयमानाश्च रुवन्तश्च महारवान् ।\nन मोहं भीमसेनस्य ददृशुः सर्वराक्षसाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though they threatened him and roared loud, none of the rakshasas saw any confusion in Bhimasena."}},{"n":50,"text":"ते शरैः क्षतसर्वाङ्गा भीमसेनभयार्दिताः ।\nभीममार्तस्वरं चक्रुर्विप्रकीर्णमहायुधाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wounded in every limb by the arrows and afflicted by fear of Bhimasena, they cried out in distress, their great weapons scattered."}},{"n":51,"text":"उत्सृज्य ते गदाशूलानसिशक्तिपरश्वधान् ।\nदक्षिणां दिशमाजग्मुस्त्रासिता दृढधन्वना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Abandoning maces, spears, swords, javelins and axes, terrified by the firm-bowed one, they fled to the south."}},{"n":52,"text":"तत्र शूलगदापाणिर्व्यूढोरस्को महाभुजः ।\nसखा वैश्रवणस्यासीन्मणिमान्नाम राक्षसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There was a broad-chested, mighty-armed friend of Vaishravana, a rakshasa called Maniman, with spear and mace in hand."}},{"n":53,"text":"अदर्शयदधीकारं पौरुषं च महाबलः ।\nस तान्दृष्ट्वा परावृत्तान्स्मयमान इवाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty one showed his authority and manliness. Seeing them turned back, he said, as if smiling:"}},{"n":54,"text":"एकेन बहवः संख्ये मानुषेण पराजिताः ।\nप्राप्य वैश्रवणावासं किं वक्ष्यथ धनेश्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Many of you have been beaten in battle by a single human. When you return to Vaishravana's abode, what will you tell the lord of wealth?\""}},{"n":55,"text":"एवमाभाष्य तान्सर्वान्न्यवर्तत स राक्षसः ।\nशक्तिशूलगदापाणिरभ्यधावच्च पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having spoken thus to all of them, that rakshasa turned back and, with javelin, spear and mace in hand, ran at the Pandava."}},{"n":56,"text":"तमापतन्तं वेगेन प्रभिन्नमिव वारणम् ।\nवत्सदन्तैस्त्रिभिः पार्श्वे भीमसेनः समर्पयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he rushed at speed like a rutting elephant, Bhimasena struck him in the flank with three calf-tooth arrows."}},{"n":57,"text":"मणिमानपि संक्रुद्धः प्रगृह्य महतीं गदाम् ।\nप्राहिणोद्भीमसेनाय परिक्षिप्य महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Maniman, furious, took a great mace and, swinging it round, hurled it at Bhimasena with great force."}},{"n":58,"text":"विद्युद्रूपां महाघोरामाकाशे महतीं गदाम् ।\nशरैर्बहुभिरभ्यर्छद्भीमसेनः शिलाशितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That huge, terrible mace, lightning-like in the air, Bhimasena cut with many stone-sharpened arrows."}},{"n":59,"text":"प्रत्यहन्यन्त ते सर्वे गदामासाद्य सायकाः ।\nन वेगं धारयामासुर्गदावेगस्य वेगिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having reached the mace, all the arrows were struck back; for all their speed they could not hold against the speed of the mace."}},{"n":60,"text":"गदायुद्धसमाचारं बुध्यमानः स वीर्यवान् ।\nव्यंसयामास तं तस्य प्रहारं भीमविक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Understanding the way of mace fighting, the mighty and fearsomely valiant Bhima turned that blow aside."}},{"n":61,"text":"ततः शक्तिं महाघोरां रुक्मदण्डामयस्मयीम् ।\nतस्मिन्नेवान्तरे धीमान्प्रजहाराथ राक्षसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, in that very moment, the wise rakshasa hurled a dreadful javelin of iron with a golden shaft."}},{"n":62,"text":"सा भुजं भीमनिर्ह्रादा भित्त्वा भीमस्य दक्षिणम् ।\nसाग्निज्वाला महारौद्रा पपात सहसा भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Roaring terribly, it pierced Bhima's right arm, flaming and very fierce, and fell suddenly to the ground."}},{"n":63,"text":"सोऽतिविद्धो महेष्वासः शक्त्यामितपराक्रमः ।\nगदां जग्राह कौरव्यो गदायुद्धविशारदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Badly wounded by the javelin, the great archer of boundless prowess, the Kaurava skilled in mace fighting, took up his mace."}},{"n":64,"text":"तां प्रगृह्योन्नदन्भीमः सर्वशैक्यायसीं गदाम् ।\nतरसा सोऽभिदुद्राव मणिमन्तं महाबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking that mace, wholly of iron, Bhima roared and charged swiftly at the mighty Maniman."}},{"n":65,"text":"दीप्यमानं महाशूलं प्रगृह्य मणिमानपि ।\nप्राहिणोद्भीमसेनाय वेगेन महता नदन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Maniman too took up a blazing great spear and hurled it at Bhimasena, roaring with great force."}},{"n":66,"text":"भङ्क्त्वा शूलं गदाग्रेण गदायुद्धविशारदः ।\nअभिदुद्राव तं तूर्णं गरुत्मानिव पन्नगम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Skilled in mace fighting, Bhima broke the spear with the tip of his mace and ran quickly at him, like Garuda at a snake."}},{"n":67,"text":"सोऽन्तरिक्षमभिप्लुत्य विधूय सहसा गदाम् ।\nप्रचिक्षेप महाबाहुर्विनद्य रणमूर्धनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Leaping into the air and suddenly whirling his mace, the mighty-armed one roared and hurled it at the head of the battle."}},{"n":68,"text":"सेन्द्राशनिरिवेन्द्रेण विसृष्टा वातरंहसा ।\nहत्वा रक्षः क्षितिं प्राप्य कृत्येव निपपात ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like a thunderbolt hurled by Indra, flung with the speed of the wind, it killed the rakshasa, reached the ground and fell like a magic spell turned back."}},{"n":69,"text":"तं राक्षसं भीमबलं भीमसेनेन पातितम् ।\nददृशुः सर्वभूतानि सिंहेनेव गवां पतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All creatures saw that rakshasa of terrible strength struck down by Bhimasena, as a lion fells the lord of cattle."}},{"n":70,"text":"तं प्रेक्ष्य निहतं भूमौ हतशेषा निशाचराः ।\nभीममार्तस्वरं कृत्वा जग्मुः प्राचीं दिशं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him slain on the ground, the surviving night-rovers cried out in distress and fled eastward."}}]}]}